Each object returned will have a self link as per  RFC9083#Section 4.2. Something like this :

  "links": [
    {
      "value": "https://example.net/route/193.254.30.0/24AS1272",
      "rel": "self",
      "href": "https://example.net/route/193.254.30.0/24AS1272",
      "type": "application/rdap+json"
    }
  ],

and for route object "origin" and "prefix"  will also have a self link too. May be I should paste whole example so it would be clearer.  What do you think?

Good point, I can make it a link to point the an autnum object. If the ASN is not registered with the registry it will redirect

for example:
```
"origin" : {
   "handle" :  "12726",
   "links": [
      {
         "value" : "https://example.com/rdap/route/XXXX",
        "rel" : "self",
        "type" : "application/rdap+json",
        "href" : "https://example.com/rdap/autnum/12726"      
      }
    ]
}"
```


What do you think?
